speech phi t
linear φ(t)
mathml <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="the sum from k equals 1 to n of k equals the fraction with numerator n open paren n plus 1 close paren and denominator 2 end fraction"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo largeop="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝑘</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>𝑛</mi></munderover><mi>𝑘</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝑛</mi><mo>⁢</mo><mrow><mo fence="true">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑛</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tekx">sum k for k from 1 to n = n(n + 1)/2</annotation></semantics></math>
speech the sum from k equals 1 to n of k equals the fraction with numerator n open paren n plus 1 close paren and denominator 2 end fraction
linear ∑_(k=1)^n k = n(n + 1)/2
mathml <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="the integral from a to b of f of x d x equals capital F of b minus capital F of a"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo largeop="true">∫</mo><mi>𝑎</mi><mi>𝑏</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true">(</mo><mi>𝑥</mi><mo fence="true">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace width="0.167em"/><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mi>𝑥</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐹</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true">(</mo><mi>𝑏</mi><mo fence="true">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐹</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true">(</mo><mi>𝑎</mi><mo fence="true">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tekx">integral of f(x) dx from a to b = F(b) - F(a)</annotation></semantics></math>
speech the integral from a to b of f of x d x equals capital F of b minus capital F of a
linear ∫_a^b f(x) dx = F(b) − F(a)
mathml <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="the limit as n approaches infinity of open paren 1 plus 1 over n close paren to the power n equals e"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>𝑛</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo fence="true">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>𝑛</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo fence="true">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝑛</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑒</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tekx">limit of (1 + 1/n)^n as n approaches infinity = e</annotation></semantics></math>
speech the limit as n approaches infinity of open paren 1 plus 1 over n close paren to the power n equals e
linear lim_(n→∞) (1 + 1/n)ⁿ = e
mathml <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="open paren a plus b close paren squared equals a squared plus 2 a b plus b squared"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo fence="true">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑎</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑏</mi></mrow><mo fence="true">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑎</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>⁢</mo><mi>𝑎</mi><mo>⁢</mo><mi>𝑏</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝑏</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tekx">(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2 a b + b^2</annotation></semantics></math>
speech open paren a plus b close paren squared equals a squared plus 2 a b plus b squared
linear (a + b)² = a² + 2ab + b²
mathml <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="equals b squared plus 2 a b plus a squared"><semantics><mrow><mrow/><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑏</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>⁢</mo><mi>𝑎</mi><mo>⁢</mo><mi>𝑏</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝑎</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tekx">= b^2 + 2 a b + a^2</annotation></semantics></math>
speech equals b squared plus 2 a b plus a squared
linear = b² + 2ab + a²
mathml <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="plus 0"><semantics><mrow><mo form="prefix">+</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tekx">+ 0</annotation></semantics></math>
speech plus 0
linear +0
mathml <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="the absolute value of x equals x if x is greater than or equal to 0; negative x otherwise"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true">|</mo><mi>𝑥</mi><mo fence="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo fence="true">{</mo><mtable columnalign="left"><mtr><mtd><mi>𝑥</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo>⁢</mo><mi>𝑥</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo form="prefix">−</mo><mi>𝑥</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mtext> otherwise </mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tekx">abs(x) = cases&#10;x    if x &gt;= 0&#10;-x   otherwise</annotation></semantics></math>
speech the absolute value of x equals x if x is greater than or equal to 0; negative x otherwise
linear |x| = cases(x if x ≥ 0; −x otherwise)
mathml <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="capital R of theta equals the 2 by 2 matrix; row 1: cosine theta, negative sine theta; row 2: sine theta, cosine theta"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true">(</mo><mi>𝜃</mi><mo fence="true">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo fence="true">(</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>𝜃</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo form="prefix">−</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>𝜃</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>𝜃</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>𝜃</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo fence="true">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tekx">R(theta) = matrix&#10;cos theta  -sin theta&#10;sin theta  cos theta</annotation></semantics></math>
speech capital R of theta equals the 2 by 2 matrix; row 1: cosine theta, negative sine theta; row 2: sine theta, cosine theta
linear R(θ) = (cos θ, −sin θ; sin θ, cos θ)
